      failed is a failing call phase, including a strict xfail that passes;
      error is a failing setup or teardown, named by the phase attribute.
    started_at, ended_at: pytest's TestReport.start of the setup phase and
      .stop of the last phase, UTC with milliseconds; tests.runs.started_at and
      ended_at.
    message: the exception as pytest summarizes it, the skip or xfail reason,
